  "term": "Charcot–Marie–Tooth disease",
  "definition": "Charcot–Marie–Tooth disease is an inherited disorder of the peripheral nerves that affects both movement and sensation. It usually causes gradually worsening wasting and reduced reflexes in the lower legs, sometimes also affecting the arms, and it is often passed down in an autosomal dominant pattern.",
